  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Coordination of the work of Caritas throughout Latin America and the Caribbean: Support to SELACC</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SELACC is the Secretariat of the Latin American and Caribbean Caritas organisations.  Its role is to strengthen the regional structure of Caritas and coordinate the work of Caritas throughout the Latin American and Caribbean Region.  In the last year SELACC has worked with the subregional Caritases to define a workplan for the period 2011-2015 (GLA 114), so that Caritas works strategically to address root causes of inequality in the region and promote respect for human rights, human dignity, and peacebuilding.  SELACC also liaises with the Department for Justice and Solidarity of the Latin American Bishops Conference.  CELAM / DEJUSOL has dedicated a whole programme area to working with Caritas in the period 2011-2015.  Through this project SELACC will continue to strengthen Caritas across the Latin America and Caribbean Region, and monitor the implementation of the workplan.</narrative>
  </description>
